__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Per-machine Claude Code settings. commit-identity.sh derives an `env.TZ`
# into this file from whoever's identity.json resolved at session start, so a
# person's declared timezone reaches the whole session instead of having to
# be retyped on every commit. It is one contributor's environment, not the
# repository's: .claude/settings.json is the tracked, shared one.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Another repository's practice text, regenerated at session start and NEVER
# committed here. tools/precedent_session_practices.py writes
# .precedent/SESSION_PRACTICES.md with the rules in force from every source
# this set declares but does not carry -- universal, whose 105 practices live
# in BestPractice's tree, not this one. Committing it would put a second copy
# of that catalogue in this history, which is the duplication shape 3 exists
# to avoid (BestPractice spec/SOURCE_SET_PROSE_GAP.md, shapes 1 and 2).
# Measured before this line existed: `git check-ignore` said not ignored, so
# the generated file was offered to the next `git add -A`.
.precedent/
